WEBVTT

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.100
The three years I spent in middle school were boring.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.780
Safe, ordinary, humdrum days, and I squandered them.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.420
Morning?

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.050
I'm a high school student as of today?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.060
I want my days in high school to be fun.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.520
Maybe... I'll join a club!

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.360
That's it!

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.360
I hear this school has lots of clubs,
and high school is all about clubs!

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.320
Clubs are youth!

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.700
And if they turn out to be boring, I can just quit!

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.410
I'm so smart!

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.130
I've always been alone,
right up through middle school.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.260
But...

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.430
In high school, I'm going to make friends
and hang out with them after school.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.890
I'm going to make the most out of high school!

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:54.320
No... maybe I'm setting the bar too high.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.900
Maybe just someone I can talk to between classes?

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.410
Anyway, my introduction today
will be crucial in achieving that.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.030
Failure is not an option!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:11.920
Okay, next.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.960
I'm Ezaki Kuriko.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.920
In middle school, I was a
sprinter in the Track Club.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.180
I plan to continue running
in the high school club, too.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.850
I don't see a single club that looks interesting...

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.980
Sure, there are a lot of them, but...

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:34.060
Maybe it would be more fun
to just join a random club?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.310
No...

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:36.820
But...

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.570
Okay, next.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.160
I'm Oohagi Botan.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.460
An old-fashioned name,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.590
a tall, slender form,

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:01.550
sleek black hair, cold eyes,

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.550
and an aura completely
unlike anyone else here...

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.850
I look forward to working with you all.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.730
That's it?

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.440
But...

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.940
It was kind of... nice and simple.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.360
Crap.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.280
I completely forgot what I'd planned to say.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.870
Okay, next.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.450
I came here from East Middle School. I'm Koike Yayoi.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.370
Oh, yeah. It was "I like video games."

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.800
It's just not right...

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:57.690
I guess for that hairstyle to work,
you really need sleek black hair.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.070
Oohagi Botan, huh?

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.740
Oohagi...

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.660
I wonder if she'd get mad
if I called her Botan-chan.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.500
I failed in my introduction,
but I still have a chance to recover.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.790
I have to start off with a lively
morning greeting to my classmates.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:26.630
It looks like Saitou in class 3 has a
crush on Ezaki from our class.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.430
Oh? Really?

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.510
M-Morning.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:30.970
Oh, good...

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.430
...morning.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.280
I'm on my own.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.860
It's only been a week since
I joined this school,

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.030
and I'm already an outcast from every clique.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.330
Is this...

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.700
Is this what they call "the wall
of high school education"?!

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:56.660
Hey, Doumyouji,

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.710
you haven't picked a club yet, right?

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.540
Want to join the Tennis Club with me?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.000
Tennis, huh?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.170
I'll think about it!

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.460
Really?

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.300
Well, hope to see you there!

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:13.180
Oohagi is always by herself...

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:16.520
Maybe she's the type that doesn't make friends?

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.020
I'd like to talk to her, but...

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.520
her desk is so far away from mine.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.150
There's never an opportunity...

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.660
It says that, at our school,

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.700
if you submit an application,
you can start whatever club you want.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.620
So I could make a club for what I want to do!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.630
But what is it I want to do, again?

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.170
It's not that there's no club
for what I want to do...

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:53.180
It's that there's nothing
I really want to do right now.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.930
I really want to do something,

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.770
but I don't know what it is...

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.600
So all I have is this restless feeling...

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.280
What is this thing I want to do?

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.320
The thing I want to do...

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:13.910
What is it?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.490
Where to do it? And with who?

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:30.260
Every time I approach others, it ends in failure.

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:35.720
I guess I'm just not cut out for this kind of thing.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.020
But if I don't approach them,

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.730
I doubt anyone will ever talk to me...

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.020
Oohagi!

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.240
Doumyouji?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.120
I caught up with you!

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:03.290
Um... listen...

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.880
Would you like to walk home together?

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.210
Wh-Why?

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.010
The reason?

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.340
Because... well...

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.140
I thought it'd be nice if we could become friends.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.260
Become... friends?

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.010
But why?

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.980
You need a reason for that, too?

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.600
Well, it was just a feeling I had, so...

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.530
Oh, I know!

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.360
Oohagi, your name's Botan, right?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.820
Yeah.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.240
I'm Sakura!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.030
They're both names of flowers!

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.120
Both... names of flowers?

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:43.910
Yup!

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.370
Peony and cherry blossom!

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.250
See? We're two of a kind!

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.000
That's why.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.420
I see.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.140
The thing I've desired for so long...

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:05.850
Sure.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.440
Let's walk home together, Sakura.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:14.740
Hooray! Since we're walking
together, want to hold hands?

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.780
Why should we?!

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:19.030
This is nothing like the image
I had in mind for a friend...

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.910
Hey, Botan-chan.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.460
Want to start a club together?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.750
That came out of nowhere.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:28.580
You don't want to?

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:32.000
It's not that I don't want to,
but what would our club do?

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:35.800
Anything!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:42.180
Let's just do everything we can
think of that sounds interesting!

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.730
What kind of plan is that?

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:47.980
Sure.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:48.980
Let's start it together.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.060
Yeah! That's the spirit!

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.570
It didn't matter to me what we did.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:58.820
As long as we were together, we could make it fun.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.200
I just had a feeling that would be the case.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.240
Wow!

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.700
So that's how you formed the club?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.370
That's wonderful, Sakura-senpai!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.790
You can shower more praise on me if you like.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.670
You told a heartwarming story?!

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:12.960
Is that not allowed?!

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.060
I didn't appear at all in the first half!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.520
I appeared all the way through!

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.650
Today, we're going to use
this hall to its fullest...

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.610
and do some super long-distance bowling!

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:39.700
Huh?

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:43.700
That confusing dream sequence
was just building up to this?!

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.160
Hold on a minute.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.700
Calm down, Sakura.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.160
We don't have any gutters.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:50.460
That's not what you should be objecting to!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.330
If we don't have any, shall I dig us some?

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.920
Please don't!

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.090
Expulsion would be the least of your worries!

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.710
That's right, Botan.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.470
Did it not occur to you that we could fill it in?

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:01.590
Fill it in?

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:04.300
Yes. Like this, for example.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.600
This creates gutters!

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.100
You can't do that either!

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:14.360
But I think that, even without gutters,

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:18.360
the distance alone should guarantee a challenge.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.780
Just like a long-distance relationship, huh?

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.910
I'll bowl the first ball!

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.700
Just be careful, okay?

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.120
What?

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.660
What is it?

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.040
Th-This is...

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.460
Looks like you're doing something fun.

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.130
Members of...

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.090
the Going Home Club.

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:45.510
Who's that?

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.850
Nat-chan, that's the Student Council President!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.480
Be on your guard! Natsuki! Karin!

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:58.400
That's the female Student Council
President who bears the alias "Kousoku"...

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.900
Takamado Reina!

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:04.070
Our Student Council President has an alias?!

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:08.990
Although the "Kousoku" in question
isn't this one, but this one.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.330
That's not very cool at all, then!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.870
I am the rulebook!

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.840
But I feel honored that
you know so much about me.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.090
"Midnight Murder..."

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.210
Oohagi Botan.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.090
She has an alias, too?!

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.720
Don't let your guard down, Natsuki.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.390
We're already in her territory.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.520
Huh? Territory?

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.430
She has a sphere of influence.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:33.480
Huh?

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:38.650
When you're on school grounds,
within her sphere of influence,

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:41.150
you become incapable of breaking rules.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.490
At the speed of light!

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:43.490
With rules!

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:44.700
She binds you!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.200
That is her power...

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.790
Handbook Bind!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.080
What?! She has superpowers?!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.540
That's right... Takamado Reina.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:58.000
It's as if she was born to become
Student Council President.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.340
That's peaking way too early in life!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:05.300
I don't think it's proper to just
decide to bowl in a public hallway.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:09.390
Going Home Club President,
Doumyouji Sakura...

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.060
No...

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.520
Grenade Rager.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.560
Perhaps that's what I should call you?

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.270
Is there a bargain sale on aliases or something?!

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:20.270
Wait a second.

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:23.860
If the president's power keeps
people from breaking the rules,

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.280
then it won't stop at bowling.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:30.910
Sakura-senpai's innocently daring skirt
length should be affected too, shouldn't it?

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.950
You catch on quick.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.080
Huh? Nothing happened.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.670
If it's just her skirt, it's not really a problem.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:41.550
Huh?

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.590
We prize self-expression among
our students, after all.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:49.010
As long as they make no extreme
alterations, we don't treat it as a problem.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.470
Right, Lady Kokonoe?

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.930
Why is she wearing a tracksuit?

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.850
And Sakura-senpai's, at that!

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.690
Actually, the official uniform is so cheap-looking,

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:03.780
I had an <i>atelier de couture</i> in Paris
make me one that looked just like it!

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.700
So she wasn't wearing our uniform at all?!

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.110
In a way, that's just an ordinary cosplay!

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.320
I thought there was something different about

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:13.490
the material that made up Claire-chan's uniform.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:16.750
The color codes were different. Did you notice?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:22.130
But does that mean, the tracksuit you
changed into was Sakura-senpai's because...

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.760
My tracksuit was made of a new
material I developed in collaboration

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.340
with a sportswear manufacturer.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.010
Is everything you own custom-made?!

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.180
Well, that said...

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.390
Whenever you want to
play like this in the future...

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.890
Just get permission before you do it.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:42.230
I'm sure we'll meet again.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.860
I'm looking forward to it.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:49.490
Um, I don't think that's really possible...

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.780
Oh? Why not?

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:54.490
Because this is the last episode!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.730
The final episode is upon us at last.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:29.530
Today, I want us to think about
how we should best address it.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.530
I think...

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.450
When I picture a final episode, I picture this.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:36.790
Our battle is only just beginning!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.450
Isn't that how you end a show that got canceled?!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.830
Perhaps episode 4 was too late for a retool.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.290
Let's save talking about what went wrong
for the wrap party at the pub!

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:48.090
I brought wasabi octopus!

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:52.130
Your understanding of pubs really
does stop there, doesn't it?

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.680
Why do you look so
pleased with yourself?!

00:15:56.890 --> 00:16:00.270
Hm... how to handle our final episode...

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:03.980
What about a stage performance
at the school festival?

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:08.980
Oh, like the conclusion to a school
anime. That could be cool.

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.820
A short skit then, maybe?

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:11.780
Why?!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:14.240
Why can't we just be a
band like in most shows?!

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.870
Forming a band for the last
episode might not be a bad idea.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:22.120
By the way, can anyone here play an instrument?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.120
The tambourine.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:26.750
The triangle.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:28.840
Death throes.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:45.150
Bang! Bang! Bang!

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:46.270
Ting.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.230
Enough!

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.480
That idea ran straight into the wall!

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:53.700
What kind of final episode do you
think we should do, Karin?

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.950
I think a touching ending would be nice.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:01.080
What about a dreamlike final episode?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.040
Oh, that sounds nice!

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:22.350
Nat-chan...

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:26.190
You were kicked by a runaway horse
on the day of the opening ceremony...

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:28.650
and have been in a coma ever since.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.440
That was three years ago.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.990
Nat-chan... Are you smiling?

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:44.000
I wonder if you're dreaming about
having fun club activities after school?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.580
You meant <i>that</i> kind of dream?!

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:48.170
The gimmick where the whole
show turns out to be a dream?!

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:52.000
But that aside, why was I the one who...

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.590
Now, now. What's the big deal?

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:57.180
A dreamlike last episode will
make us the talk of the Net.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:58.800
Who cares?!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.390
Dreamlike seal!

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:06.350
What we "should" do shouldn't be
determined by what people want to see.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.560
It's the final episode, so to ensure we have no regrets,

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.560
let's figure out what we <i>want </i>to do!

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:13.690
This from the girl who always
does what she wants anyway?!

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.490
What we want to do, huh?

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:19.450
In that case, I want to settle
things with the Four Kings.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:23.200
Oh! Settling your battle of destiny once and for all!

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.410
That's right.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:27.660
I have to defeat the one I didn't beat before.

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.330
You meant the Four <i>Bear </i>Kings, didn't you?!

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:36.420
If we get to do what we want to do,
then I'd like a final episode like this.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:45.970
Claire-senpai, the Earth has gotten so far away...

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:47.890
Changes to Earth's climate,

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:49.940
rampant disease,

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.810
the outbreak of another world war...

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:58.900
Our Mother Earth can no
longer support human life.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:03.580
So you and I are really the last humans alive...

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.830
This ship will travel on autopilot,

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.750
searching for a world that can support human life.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.290
Karin.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:17.380
You and I will become the Eve
and Eve of that new world.

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:19.630
Claire-senpai...

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.630
Karin...

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.430
Claire-senpai...

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:25.970
That's too grand a scale!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:29.350
And if you just have Eve and Eve, that
new world's never going to have a future!

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:32.230
We can make it all work out
somehow, using iPS cells.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:35.900
It disturbs me that it doesn't
sound like a joke coming from her.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:38.990
What about you, Karin?

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.450
Let me see...

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.160
What I want to do for the last episode...

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.490
is chat with all of you,

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.910
eat sweets,

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:50.500
then, stop by the convenience
store on my way home.

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:53.710
But that's what we always do!

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.290
Yes. I want to do what we always do.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.050
What we always do...

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.170
That could be nice, too!

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:04.720
Then, I think it's time to
go home like we always do!

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.220
Let's stop by the convenience store...

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.470
Buy sweets...

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:08.640
And go to the park!

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.970
Hooray!

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.320
Come in!

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.070
Excuse us!

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:45.610
Your membership is approved!

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:49.370
Using milk...

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.280
A toast!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.910
So this is wasabi octopus!

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.830
You pushed for it without
knowing what it was?!

00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:59.000
Now, now.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.920
No need to scold her for
something that's in the past.

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:07.590
But when I think that this is
the end, it feels a little lonely.

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:09.550
That's right.

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:12.100
All we have left is to do the preview.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:14.220
Huh? Preview?

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:17.560
If this is the last episode,
why is there a preview?

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:20.730
Sakura said it with such confidence,

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:23.610
I was convinced that this
was the last episode, but...

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:25.230
You don't think...

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:26.400
Now that you mention it,

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:30.160
there was that time she confused
episode 4 for episode 3, too.

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:33.370
Which means...

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:36.870
A-Anyone can make mistakes, right?!

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:40.830
I'm sorry!

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:42.000
See you next week!

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:44.170
It's <i>not</i> all well!

00:22:45.300 --> 00:22:46.300
Did you all know?

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.930
This week's Chronicles of the Going
Home Club wasn't the last episode!

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:53.020
Next week is Record 37: Misreading.

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:56.520
And about twenty more... are you kidding?!

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:57.810
We'll go flat out to get through them all!

00:22:57.810 --> 00:22:59.020
Hope you enjoy them!
